@ 10.1.2.5 - Proto-Philippine to Ifugao
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Llamzon, Teodoro A. (1975), “Proto-Philippine Phonology”. Archipel 9(1):29 – 42; and from other changes and information from this document
	ə → o
	*j → ɡ / _#
	{z,*Z,*D,*j} → d
	# *R seems to have had a few different reflexes, mainly one of /l ɡ j/; if /ɡ j/ occurred, /ɡ/ was more probable at word boundaries and /j/ was more probable medially
	{q,h} → ∅
	{s,c} → h
	∅ → j / _iw#
	ay → e / _#